.TH GENV 1 "August 2026" "genv 4.0.12" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
genv \\- global environment manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genv
<command> [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Track, sync, and reproduce your software environment across macOS, Windows,
Arch Linux, Ubuntu-like Linux, and WSL2. Desired state lives in
.I genv.json
; applied state lives in a machine-local lock file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add <id> [flags]
Add a package to the spec and install it now. Persist only after a successful install.
.TP
.B remove <id>
Remove a package from the spec and uninstall it now. Alias: rm.
.TP
.B adopt <id> [flags]
Track an already-installed package without reinstalling.
.TP
.B disown <id>
Stop tracking a package without uninstalling it.
.TP
.B scan [flags]
Discover installed packages and bulk-adopt them. Use --dry-run / --yes.
.TP
.B status [flags]
Show drift between the spec, lock file, and live system.
.TP
.B list
List packages recorded in the lock file. Alias: ls.
.TP
.B apply [flags]
Reconcile system state with genv.json.
.TP
.B validate
Validate genv.json and genv-managed agent executables.
.TP
.B upgrade [flags]
Upgrade outdated tracked packages. --all upgrades every unconstrained package.
.TP
.B updates <check|start|stop|status>
Managed updates checker.
.TP
.B migrate [flags]
Convert v1–v7 host-scoped specs to schema v8 targets.
.TP
.B export [flags]
Write a single-target snapshot plus report.
.TP
.B map [flags]
Print assist-only manager mapping suggestions.
.TP
.B profile <list|create|switch>
Named overlays. Refused on schemaVersion 8 specs.
.TP
.B pull
Fetch genv.json and relative files assets from repo.url.
.TP
.B init
Create a new schemaVersion 8 genv.json.
.TP
.B edit
Open genv.json in $EDITOR.
.TP
.B env / shell / service / files
Manage env vars, aliases, user services, and file adopt.
.TP
.B completion
Print or install bash, zsh, fish, or powershell completion.
.TP
.B clean [\\-\\-dry\\-run]
Clear detected package-manager caches.
.TP
.B version
Show genv build version information.
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.SH COMMON FLAGS
.TP
.B \\-\\-file <path>
Path to genv.json (default under ~/.config/genv/).
.TP
.B \\-\\-lock-file <path>
Path to the lock file (default ~/.config/genv/genv.lock.json).
.TP
.B \\-\\-target <id>
Schema v8 target (default: $GENV_TARGET or host classification).
.TP
.B \\-\\-host <name>
Legacy host filter for v1–v7 records (classification, not hostname).
.SH COMMAND-SPECIFIC FLAGS
.SS add / adopt
.TP
.B \\-\\-version <ver>
Version constraint, e.g. "0.10.*"
.TP
.B \\-\\-prefer <mgr>
Preferred manager, e.g. brew or apt
.TP
.B \\-\\-manager <mgr:name,...>
Manager-specific package names, e.g. snap:hello,brew:hello
.SS apply
.TP
.B \\-\\-dry\\-run
Print the reconcile plan without executing
.TP
.B \\-\\-strict
Exit with an error if any package cannot be resolved
.TP
.B \\-\\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
.B \\-\\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON to stdout
.TP
.B \\-\\-force / \\-\\-backup
Overwrite mismatched files; keep timestamped backups
.TP
.B \\-\\-force-new-lock
Back up a foreign lock and start a new local lock
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
bad arguments or unknown command
.TP
.B 2
filesystem or serialization error
.TP
.B 3
genv.json fails schema validation
.TP
.B 4
semantic error — also returned by \\fBgenv status\\fR when drift exists
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/genv/genv.json
Desired-state specification. Commit this.
.TP
.B ~/.config/genv/genv.lock.json
Applied-state lock. Machine-local; never commit.
.SH AUTHOR
Karim Smires and contributors.
